      "insight_cloud": {
        "type": "fact",
        "title": "Anhedonia vs. Sadness",
        "text": "Anhedonia is the clinical term for the inability to feel pleasure. While sadness is an active emotion, anhedonia is the presence of an emotional 'void'. It's often linked to the brain's reward system status.",
